        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-23T17:06:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The documentation of I2C_Api_MasterWrite states that the return is a \"common error code\", which I assume means EC_ series error codes.  So what is the point of \"hiding\" the particular error here, and always returning EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN.  In my opinion, you could just have\nreturn I2C_Api_Master...(...)\nin each branch, dropping both status and ret variables.",
      "revId": "008bf25cf3a197ff615176dc930d746b5c582db2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e1a21e6_344bd4e9",
        "filename": "chip/max32660/i2c_chip.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T18:02:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did simplify this to return if the I2C_Api_Master..(...) is not successful.... but I don\u0027t think I can just do a return I2C_Api_Master...(...) here, if I did then the following I2C_Api_MasterRead would never be given a chance to execute.",
      "parentUuid": "315d4725_fdbe21ea",
      "revId": "008bf25cf3a197ff615176dc930d746b5c582db2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ac8aac8_033df1de",
        "filename": "chip/max32660/i2c_chip.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1289152
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T20:38:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think just returning `status` in the error case would be fine here, as I can\u0027t imagine we\u0027d want to carry on with the read if the write failed.",
      "parentUuid": "9e1a21e6_344bd4e9",
      "revId": "008bf25cf3a197ff615176dc930d746b5c582db2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b82b59c_6f3a79e2",
        "filename": "chip/max32660/i2c_chip.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
